    <sys:String x:Key="Str.Info.HowToText">Add a folder with photos using the + button in the Library section; the app indexes it, including subfolders, without modifying or copying any file.|Select a folder in the tree to see only its photos (including subfolders); click the “Library” title to show all photos again.|Double-click a photo (or press Enter) to open it full screen; zoom with the mouse wheel, pan by dragging.|Right-click a source folder: Rescan (new / deleted photos) or Remove from library.|Source folders and the theme can also be managed from Options (gear icon).|Select one or more photos (Ctrl / Shift + click, Ctrl+A), then right-click → Add to album / Add tag. Click the “Albums” title to see albums as a grid of cards; double-click opens an album.|The selected photo's tags appear in the right panel: “+” adds, “×” removes. Click a tag on the left to see all photos that have it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str.Info.Shortcuts">Keyboard shortcuts</sys:String>
